{"url": "https://www.ccny.cuny.edu/admissions/chemical-engineering", "final_url": "https://www.ccny.cuny.edu/admissions/chemical-engineering", "status": 200, "method": "chromium", "fetched": "2026-11-13", "text": "Need Any Help?\nHello! I am an automated chatbot who can help answer your questions about CCNY.\nHow can I help you?\nSkip to main content\nSEARCH\nLOGIN\nABOUT\nACADEMICS\nADMISSIONS\nRESEARCH\nSTUDENT AFFAIRS\nSUPPORT CCNY\nADMISSIONS\nHOME\nTOURS AND INFO SESSIONS\nUNDERGRADUATE ADMISSIONS\nGRADUATE ADMISSIONS\nChemical Engineering\nHome\n/\nDivision of Enrollment Management\n/\nAdmissions\n/\nChemical Engineering\nTurn scientific knowledge into solutions for the challenges shaping our world. The Chemical Engineering graduate programs at The City College of New York offer opportunities for advanced study and research at both the master\u2019s and doctoral levels, with an emphasis on developing the technical expertise and innovative thinking needed to address complex problems in engineering and the sciences.\nStudents build advanced knowledge in chemical engineering while engaging in research that connects fundamental principles with real-world applications. Through rigorous coursework, hands-on research, and close collaboration with faculty, students develop skills in analysis, experimentation, problem-solving, and innovation.\nAdmissions Facts\nChemical Engineering - ME\nTotal Credits: 31\nGRE Required: No\nMinimum Language Test Scores: 79-80 (TOEFL IBT), 4.5 (TOEFL updated scale), 6.5 (IELTS), 53 (PTE) or 100 (Duolingo)\nDegree Awarded: M.E.\nSupporting Documents Required:\nOfficial transcripts from all post-secondary institutions attended\n2 letters of recommendation from people familiar with your technical ability\nResume/CV\nPersonal Statement\nThis program does not except Non-Degree applications\nProgram Advisor: Prof. Carol Steiner\nchemeinfo@ccny.cuny.edu\nFor more information, please visit the Program Website.\nChemical Engineering - Ph.D.\nTotal Credits: 61\nGRE Required: Not required\nMinimum Language Test Scores: 79-80 (TOEFL IBT), 4.5 (TOEFL updated scale), 6.5 (IELTS), 53 (PTE) or 100 (Duolingo)\nDegree Awarded: Ph.D.\nSupporting Documents Required:\nOfficial transcripts from all post-secondary institutions attended\n3letters of recommendation\nResume/CV\nPersonal Statement\nProgram Advisor: Prof. Charles Maldarelli\nFor more information, please visit the Program Website and/or contact Jennifer Harrington, Academic Advising Manager, at jharrington@ccny.cuny.edu\nFor more information, please visit the Program Website.\nReady to Take the Next Step?\nApplication Process Admissions Deadlines Apply Today\nCONTACT INFORMATION\nWille Administration Building\nRoom 101\n160 Convent Avenue\nNew York, NY 10031\n212.650.6977\ngraduateadmissions@ccny.cuny.edu\nKEEP IN TOUCH WITH US!\nSign up to connect with Graduate Admissions and receive information about our graduate programs, upcoming events, application deadlines, and more.\nConnect With Us!\nIN-PERSON OFFICE HOURS\nMonday, Tuesday, Thursday, and Friday 9:00 AM - 5:00 PM\nWednesday 9:00 AM - 6:30 PM\nReserve your place in line now\nVIRTUAL FRONT DESK HOURS\nMonday and Thursday 10:00 AM - 1:00 PM\nTuesday 2:30 PM - 6:30 PM\nWednesday and Friday Closed\nSchedule your virtual appointment now\nLast Updated: 09/22/2026 09:33\nWe use cookies and other tracking technologies to improve your browsing experience on our website, analyze our website traffic, and understand where our visitors are coming from. If you choose \"ACCEPT ALL\", you consent to the use of all cookies. You can accept and reject individual cookie types and revoke your consent for the future at any time at \"Settings\".\nPrivacy policy\nAbout us\nCOOKIE SETTINGS\nDENY ALL\nACCEPT ALL\nThe City College of New York\n160 Convent Avenue New York, NY 10031\np: 212.650.7000\nSTUDENTS\nEmail\nAcademic Calendar\nCourses - CCNY Bulletin\nCourses - CUNY list\nApply Now - Undergraduate\nApply Now - Graduate\nL